{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"8e1a4c498e3f76010419866815b8638d0f6becba1009f62497513a8148004958","digest":{"component_or_area":"Jira reconciler inbound-apply surface","key_entities":["src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_events.py","_inbound_update_write_status_event","_inbound_create_write_status_event","_cascade_inbound_status_parents","rebar._commands.transition._CASCADING_EDGES","rebar._commands.transition._resolve_parent_in_status","_write_event_file","docs/concurrency.md","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_inbound_status_cascade.py"],"problem_keywords":["parent-first cascade","status invariant","inbound reconcile","closed parent","active child","parity gap"],"propositions":["Inbound Jira status updates write STATUS events directly without cascading to ancestors, bypassing the parent-first cascade invariant enforced in interactive verbs.","The parent-first cascade must be uniformly applied across all write surfaces (interactive and inbound reconcile) such that no non-terminal-state ticket can be a child of a closed ticket.","The inbound-apply path must share the interactive cascade DECISION (cascading edge table and parent-eligibility logic) but use its own deterministic write primitive, not route through transition_compute.","Inbound status changes to active states must recursively cascade parent STATUS events up the chain (topmost first) before writing the child, with cycle guards and no-op suppression for batch idempotency."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787884718091535001,"uuid":"ddaaf6e5-8b38-4c2c-a1d8-f627babf415c"}